plain:   The entry channel and the staff channel must be different.
model:   [Fixed("The entry channel and the staff channel must be different.")]

## honeypot_channel_missing
discord: Choose the honeypot channel.
plain:   Choose the honeypot channel.
model:   [Fixed("Choose the honeypot channel.")]

## honeypot_rule_missing
discord: Choose the rule the honeypot applies.
plain:   Choose the rule the honeypot applies.
model:   [Fixed("Choose the rule the honeypot applies.")]

## honeypot_rule_required_fields
discord: The rule **Honeypot** has required context fields, which the honeypot can't fill in. Choose another rule or make those fields optional.
plain:   The rule Honeypot has required context fields, which the honeypot can't fill in. Choose another rule or make those fields optional.
model:   [Fixed("The rule "), Bold([User("Honeypot")]), Fixed(" has required context fields, which the honeypot can't fill in. Choose another rule or make those fields optional.")]

## activity_no_route
discord: Choose a channel for server activity.
plain:   Choose a channel for server activity.
model:   [Fixed("Choose a channel for server activity.")]

## activity_needs_audit_log
discord: Quack needs the View Audit Log permission to show who banned or unbanned a member.
plain:   Quack needs the View Audit Log permission to show who banned or unbanned a member.
model:   [Fixed("Quack needs the View Audit Log permission to show who banned or unbanned a member.")]

## channel_permissions
discord: Quack needs Manage Messages and Read Message History in <#444>.
plain:   Quack needs Manage Messages and Read Message History in #staff.
model:   [Fixed("Quack needs Manage Messages and Read Message History in "), Channel(ChannelRef { id: ChannelId(444), name: Some("staff") }), Fixed(".")]

## channel_not_staff_only
discord: <#444> isn't staff-only.
plain:   #staff isn't staff-only.
model:   [Channel(ChannelRef { id: ChannelId(444), name: Some("staff") }), Fixed(" isn't staff-only.")]

